[issue.1537]
number = 1537
title = "[Coherence] The VerificationStatus declaration is added only by the Rust sdkgen splice, so generate_jvm.py --check now rejects the committed GeneratedSchema.java and platform-sdk-check fails"
revision = "210639d0360c53f5c2fdd81c9c7c5e84b24b8c84"
verdict = "task"
evidence = "At revision 210639d0360c53f5c2fdd81c9c7c5e84b24b8c84, services/agent/schema/agent-api/v1.kvx:121 defines VerificationStatus only through verification_status prose, which sdk/platform/generators/generate_jvm.py:185 does not treat as fields and render_models at sdk/platform/generators/generate_jvm.py:391 therefore omits, while commit c5867b3753e6284fcd8f40e70a26376320726274 added the independent Rust renderer at sdk/platform/generators/src/main.rs:1491 and splice at sdk/platform/generators/src/main.rs:1547 with check/write callers at sdk/platform/generators/src/main.rs:1999 and sdk/platform/generators/src/main.rs:2014, leaving the 28-line declaration at sdk/platform/jvm/src/main/java/com/sidiora/layerx/sdk/GeneratedSchema.java:1028 inconsistent with Python's byte comparison at sdk/platform/generators/generate_jvm.py:564, required by services/platform/Makefile.inc:233 and sdk/platform/conformance/run-jvm.sh:12, and untested by the Rust-only splice comparison at sdk/platform/generators/tests/drift.rs:837."
close_comment = "The JVM schema generators disagree about VerificationStatus, causing the Python drift check to reject the committed schema. The follow-up task makes the Python generator the declaration's source and adds a regression check that both generators accept the same schema while retaining all status validation."

